---
import FutureConceptDisclosure from './FutureConceptDisclosure.astro';
import FutureConceptQuestions from './FutureConceptQuestions.astro';
import { ownerWorkspaceQuestions } from '../data/future-concepts';

const attention = [['01', 'Today’s overview', 'A focused place for site visits, follow-ups, reminders, and tasks.'], ['02', 'Lead & estimate pipeline', 'A possible view of requests moving toward a site visit or estimate.'], ['03', 'Upcoming work', 'A concise schedule-shaped view without replacing the calendar of record.'], ['04', 'Active jobs', 'A simple way to see work that needs a status or next-step review.'], ['05', 'Estimates & follow-up', 'A way to surface conversations that may need attention.'], ['06', 'Reviews & follow-up', 'A future place to review post-job follow-up without automating it.']];
---
<section class="future-concept future-concept--owner" aria-labelledby="owner-workspace-title">
  <header class="future-concept__hero">
    <p class="future-v1__kicker">Business workflow concept</p>
    <h1 id="owner-workspace-title">One useful view of work needing attention.</h1>
    <p>Owner Workspace explores a future place to review exceptions and next steps without rebuilding the systems that already work for East Coast Foam.</p>
    <FutureConceptDisclosure />
  </header>

  <nav class="future-concept__switcher" aria-label="Business workflow concepts"><a aria-current="page" href="/future/owner">Owner Workspace</a><a href="/future/capture">Project Capture &amp; Publish</a></nav>

  <figure class="future-concept__vision">
    <figcaption><div><p class="future-v1__kicker">Concept vision</p><h2>Reference direction for discussion.</h2></div><p>Supplied visual reference shown to make the intended dashboard rhythm and mobile companion view easier to evaluate. The pictured content is illustrative only.</p></figcaption>
    <img src="/images/concepts/owner-workspace-reference.png" alt="Owner Workspace visual concept reference showing a dark desktop workspace and mobile companion layout" loading="eager" />
  </figure>

  <section class="future-concept__workspace" aria-labelledby="owner-coded-title">
    <div class="future-concept__workspace-bar"><span>East Coast Foam</span><b>Illustrative static view</b><span>Today</span></div>
    <div class="future-concept__workspace-title"><div><p>How this could work</p><strong id="owner-coded-title">A clearer view of what may need attention.</strong></div><a href="/future/capture">Explore Project Capture <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    <div class="future-concept__workspace-grid">
      {attention.map(([number, title, text]) => <article><span>{number}</span><h2>{title}</h2><p>{text}</p><small>Illustrative only — no live business data</small></article>)}
    </div>
    <div class="future-concept__workspace-foot"><span>Nothing here is connected to estimates, accounting, calendar, messages, reviews, or storage.</span><span>Validate before building.</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="future-concept__value" aria-labelledby="owner-value-title">
    <div><p class="future-v1__kicker">The product hypothesis</p><h2 id="owner-value-title">Make exceptions easier to see, not another system to manage.</h2></div>
    <div><p>A future workspace could help surface the few things that need a decision or follow-up. It should leave the source-of-truth systems in place unless there is a real reason to change them.</p><a href="/future/capture">See the related Project Capture concept <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
  </section>

  <FutureConceptQuestions questions={ownerWorkspaceQuestions} title="Would this solve a real daily problem?" />
</section>
